==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fa|en}} {{term|sc=fa-Arab|ستان|tr=stān|lang=fa}} and {{etyl|sa|en}} {{term|sc=Deva|स्थान|tr=sthā́na|lang=sa}}, both deriving from common [[Indo-Iranian]] verbal stem {{term|तिष्ठति|sc=unicode|√sthā|to stand, stay|lang=sa}}, from Proto-Indo-European {{recons|steh₂-||to stand|lang=ine-pro}}, whence also English verbs {{term|stay|lang=en}} and {{term|stand|lang=en}}.

===Suffix===
'''-stan'''

# [[home]] of; [[place]] where one [[stay]]s; used especially in place names

